    "name": "E2E HubSpot - Enroll Contact In Workflow",
    "notes": {
        "c41d8373-05b9-4237-9010-cd256d24dff9": {
            "x": 72,
            "y": -85,
            "width": 470,
            "height": 300,
            "content": "ENVIRONMENT \u2014 this flow is built for:\n- Appmixer account: auth+hubspot@appmixer.com (service appmixer:hubspot)\n- HubSpot portal: 148964607 (developer test account, EU, accountType DEVELOPER_TEST)\n- Portal asset: contact workflow 71431203 (v2/v3 id) 'E2E Enroll Test Workflow'\n\nMANUAL PREREQUISITES \u2014 this flow needs a HubSpot portal with workflows:\n1) Workflows are a Professional/Enterprise feature. Use a developer test account (accountType DEVELOPER_TEST) or any Pro+ portal; on free/STANDARD portals the workflows API returns 403 'workflows-access-public-api' regardless of OAuth scopes.\n2) The portal must contain at least one ACTIVE contact-based workflow (create one in Automation > Workflows). The flow enrolls a fresh contact into the first workflow returned by GET /automation/v4/flows.\n3) The connected account must include the 'automation' scope (hubspot bundle >= 4.8.0).\n4) The workflowId in the Enroll component and the sanity-check GET URL are pinned to the test portal's workflow \u2014 update both when porting to another portal. Use the v2/v3 workflow id (GET /automation/v2/workflows), NOT the v4 flows id \u2014 the v2 enrollment endpoint parses workflowId as a 32-bit integer and rejects v4 ids."
        }
    },
    "type": "automation"
